{
  "uid": "saakshi-estate-health",
  "title": "SAAKSHI \u00b7 Estate Health",
  "description": "Per-camera connectivity, trust and health across the estate, plus observed uptime against the stated >99% target.",
  "tags": ["saakshi", "estate"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": false,
  "refresh": "15s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this board claims, and what it does not",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Uptime here is measured, not targeted.** The left-hand stat is `avg_over_time(up{job=\"saakshi-api\"}[$__range]) * 100` \u2014 the fraction of scrapes in the *dashboard's own time range* that reached the API. The stat beside it is the stated PROJECT.md target of **> 99%**, drawn as a separate number so the two can never be confused. If the observed figure is below the target, this board says so.\n\n**Estate availability is a different question from ours.** `saakshi_estate_camera_uptime_ratio` is the fraction of *probed* cameras whose newest health check was connectable \u2014 a property of the department's estate and its network, not of this software. A camera that has never been probed is in neither number."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Observed API uptime (this time range)",
      "description": "Measured from Prometheus' own scrape results over the dashboard's range. Red below the stated 99% target. Short ranges are noisy by construction: one missed scrape in a 10-minute window is 2.5%.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 5,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 99
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 3
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "avg_over_time(up{job=\"saakshi-api\"}[$__range]) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "observed",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "format": "time_series",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Stated target",
      "description": "PROJECT.md's stated benchmark. A constant, exported so the panel next to it can be compared against something written down rather than remembered. Wrapped in max() so a stale series from a process that has restarted can never draw the threshold twice.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 5,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 5
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "saakshi-prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(saakshi_uptime_target_ratio) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "target",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "format": "time_series",
          "refId": "E"
        }
      ]
    },
